; DOMAIN: fargues-fontaine-curve [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: The Fargues-Fontaine curve X_FF (for a fixed complete algebraically closed nonarchimedean field F of characteristic p, e.g. F=C_p^flat) is the complete curve X = Proj(P) where P = bigoplus_{d>=0} B^{phi=p^d} is the graded ring of Frobenius-eigenvectors in Fontaine's ring B (period ring), or equivalently the adic/schematic curve whose closed points are the untilts F^sharp of F up to Frobenius (Spa A_inf minus its two extreme points, quotiented by phi^Z). X_FF is a complete Dedekind-like curve: regular Noetherian of Krull dimension 1, with H^0(X,O)=Q_p and no global functions of positive degree, functioning as the geometric object over which p-adic Galois representations become vector bundles. The classification theorem (Fargues-Fontaine, Kedlaya): vector bundles on X_FF are classified by their Harder-Narasimhan slopes; every bundle is a direct sum of stable bundles O(lambda), lambda in Q, where O(d/h) is the stable bundle of rank h and degree d (slope lambda=d/h). Semistable of slope 0 <=> trivial <=> unramified/crystalline period data; the Newton polygon = HN polygon. The diamond X_FF^diamond parametrizes untilts and is the base for the stack Bun_G of G-bundles on X_FF; the semistable-Newton stratification of Bun_G (with the Kottwitz set B(G) of phi-conjugacy classes indexing strata) is the geometric incarnation of the local Langlands / geometrization program (Fargues-Scholze).
; Bridge: genesis_diamond (X_FF^diamond is a diamond; its points ARE the untilts parametrized on Perf, and Bun_G is a v-stack of G-bundles over the FF curve living on the diamond/v-site — the FF curve is the curve whose diamond realizes the untilt moduli) + genesis_perfectoid (points of X_FF = untilts F^sharp of the perfectoid tilt F, so the curve is glued from perfectoid/A_inf period data, B built from W(O_F)) + genesis_sheaf_cohomology (vector bundles + HN filtration + coherent cohomology on X_FF; H^0/H^1 of O(lambda) give the period/Galois-cohomology computations, and Bun_G sheaf cohomology drives Fargues-Scholze).
(= (fargues-fontaine-curve $F) (proj (graded-ring (map $d (frobenius-eigenspace (period-ring $F) (power $p $d))))))
(= (closed-points (fargues-fontaine-curve $F)) (quotient (untilts $F) (frobenius-action)))
(= (bundle-classification (fargues-fontaine-curve $F)) (direct-sum (map $lambda (stable-bundle (O $lambda)))))
(= (stable-bundle (O (slope $d $h))) (bundle (rank $h) (degree $d) (slope (div $d $h))))
(= (harder-narasimhan $E) (newton-polygon (slopes $E)))
(= (global-sections (O 0)) (Q-p))
(= (bun-G-over-ff $G) (v-stack (G-bundles (fargues-fontaine-curve $F))))
(= (newton-stratification (bun-G-over-ff $G)) (indexed-by (kottwitz-set $G)))